Switchboard's design draws on ideas from these open-source projects. No
source code is copied from them; they are credited because their designs
shaped this one:

  - MetaMCP (https://github.com/metatool-ai/metamcp), MIT License:
    namespaces exposed as endpoints, per-tool overrides, a composable
    middleware pipeline.
  - MCPJungle (https://github.com/mcpjungle/mcpjungle), MPL-2.0:
    tool groups built from included servers and tools minus excluded tools,
    and re-checking access when a tool is called.
  - Docker MCP Gateway (https://github.com/docker/mcp-gateway), MIT License:
    profiles, a table of AI client configuration files, and routing on the
    MCP client name.
  - Cloudflare Agents Code Mode (https://github.com/cloudflare/agents),
    MIT License: exposing MCP tools to model-written code as typed
    functions, result unwrapping and structural truncation.
  - Bifrost (https://github.com/maximhq/bifrost), Apache License 2.0:
    code mode enabled per client and execution budgets.
